# Aston Martin 15/98 open sports tourer, 1937-1939.
#
# The 15/98: the 2-litre-engined touring model with the longer, roomier body
# and the open four-seat tourer coachwork. The open tourer is modelled.
#
# Dimensions: NO reliable published figure was found. The model measures
# 4.23 x 1.61 x 1.38 m with the hood folded, on a 2.75 m wheelbase,
# ESTIMATED from the photographs and assumed tyre outside diameters; these are
# not specifications and must not be quoted as such. This is the works tourer
# with the hood folded.
#
# Shape reference: a black 15/98 open sports tourer, plate EOL 500, in near
# true side elevation, front three-quarter and rear three-quarter.
#
# Colours: grade (d). No British colour list exists; the car was finished to
# order. The objects carry plain names (green, black, red, silver).
#
# Speed 140 km/h, an estimate for the touring body. Comfort 35/383 on the
# line 330 + 1.5 x 35: an open tourer with four seats, more comfortable than
# the two-seat sports cars. Classes 2,3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 1937 intro, retires staggered 1956-1959.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-15-98.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-15-98.dae. References:
# citycars/references/aston-15-98/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear wings do not sweep far enough down, the
# folded hood and fuel tank are simplified, the external exhaust is too
# prominent, and plate lettering is absent. At 128 px the four-seat tourer
# proportions, tall grille, auxiliary lamps and inclined spare read as a
# 15/98.


obj=citycar
